{
 "comment001": "KindleHub. Lives in KUAL rather than the book library on purpose:",
 "comment002": "the content indexer classifies loose .sh files as personal documents",
 "comment003": "and drops them out of a Books-filtered library view, which made them",
 "comment004": "appear and then vanish one by one. KUAL reads this file directly and",
 "comment005": "never consults the indexer.",
 "comment006": "exitmenu is true throughout because every script draws its own",
 "comment007": "full-screen output with fbink, and the KUAL menu would cover it.",
 "comment008": "This file needs config.xml beside it. Without config.xml, KUAL does",
 "comment009": "not read the extension at all and the menu never appears.",
